<title>USA: US meat production 0.1 pct below week ago-USDA.</title>
<headline>US meat production 0.1 pct below week ago-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Red meat production for week</p>
<p>ending Saturday, Dec 14 fell 0.1 pct at 825.5 min lbs.-USDA</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING/1  BEEF   CALF/VEAL   PORK/2  LAMB/MUTTON TOTALS/3</p>
<p>14-Dec-96	474.8     6.2	 339.2	5.3	825.5</p>
<p>07-Dec-96	474.1     6.4	 340.7	5.0	826.2</p>
<p>Change:	   0.2%    -3.1%	 -0.4%     6.0%	-0.1%</p>
<p>16-Dec-95	465.3     6.3	 353.0	5.8	830.4</p>
<p>Change:	   2.0%    -1.6%	 -3.9%    -8.6%	-0.6%</p>
<p>1996 YTD:    23961.4   336.8     16058.4    246.8    40603.4</p>
<p>1995 YTD:    23726.3   286.7     16815.3    265.5    41093.8</p>
<p>Change:	   1.0%    17.5%	 -4.5%    -7.0%	-1.2%</p>
<p>LIVESTOCK SLAUGHTER (HEAD)</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING   CATTLE   CALVES/VEALERS     HOGS     SHEEP/LAMBS</p>
<p>14-Dec-96     694,000	   30,000     1,798,000	83,000</p>
<p>07-Dec-96     692,000	   31,000     1,817,000	80,000</p>
<p>Change:	   0.3%	    -3.2%	   -1.0%	  3.8%</p>
<p>16-Dec-95     655,000	   30,000     1,891,000	92,000</p>
<p>Change:	   6.0%	     0.0%	   -4.9%	 -9.8%</p>
<p>1996 YTD:  34,245,000	1,623,000    86,720,000   3,855,000</p>
<p>1995 YTD:*  33,625,000	1,336,000    90,690,000   4,230,000</p>
<p>Change:	   1.8%	    21.5%	   -4.4%	 -8.9%</p>
<p>*1995 slaughter totals adjusted to reflect NASS revisions</p>
<p>AVERAGE WEIGHTS (LBS.)</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING  LIVE CATTLE    CALVES/VEALERS  HOGS  SHEEP/LAMBS</p>
<p>14-Dec-96    Est    1169	     355	259	  128</p>
<p>07-Dec-96    Est    1170	     355	259	  127</p>
<p>16-Dec-95    Actual 1198	     362	257	  127</p>
<p>Dressed</p>
<p>14-Dec-96    Est     687	     209	189	   64</p>
<p>07-Dec-96    Est     688	     209	188	   63</p>
<p>16-Dec-95    Actual  718	     211	187	   63</p>
<p>FOR THE WEEK PERCENTAGE OF TOTAL CATTLE SLAUGHTERED BY CLASS</p>
<p>ENDING	   STEERS	HEIFERS	COWS     BULLS &amp; STAGS</p>
<p>30-Nov-96	46.7%	   30.2%	21.4%	  1.8%</p>
<p>02-Dec-95	47.8%	   27.8%	22.5%	  2.0%</p>
